.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rars-repair 1 "" rars
.SH NAME
rars\-repair \- Repair a damaged archive using its recovery record
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrars repair\fR [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Repair a damaged archive using its recovery record
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
Archive password (visible in process list \[u2014] prefer \-\-password\-file or the TTY prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads for parallel compression and extraction (default: all available cores)
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read password from file ("\-" for stdin); trailing newlines are stripped
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
Progress reporting mode for long\-running operations
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Either <archive> <repaired\-archive>, or <rar\-parts\-and\-rev\-files...> <outdir>
